'''''Narcissus assoanus''''', the  '''rush-leaf jonquil''', is a perennial [[bulb|bulbous plant]] native to [[Spain]] and [[France]]; it is now naturalized in [[Turkey]].<ref>[http://apps.kew.org/wcsp/namedetail.do?name_id=282799 Kew World Checklist of Selected Plant Families]</ref> It grows to 15&nbsp;cm (6&nbsp;in) in height and has yellow flowers with a slightly lemony fragrance.<ref>[https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/page/736189#page/275/mode/1up Schult. & Schult.f. 1830. Systema Vegetabilium 7(2): 962.]</ref> Subspecies include ''N. assoanus'' subsp. ''assoanus'' and ''N. assoanus'' subsp. ''praelongus''.

